      "index": 4,
      "role": "user",
      "text": "In the new sources provided, Amanda is mentioned only in the transcript \"The Cat With A Hole In Reality\".\nAccording to this source, Amanda is a figure used to ground the abstract concepts of the Scalar-Angular-Twist (SAT) theory in human emotion and experience\nlock\n. She is described as being very isolated and struggling\nlock\n. The text explains her behavior—specifically keeping lights and music on 24/7 and surrounding herself with uranium glass—as a subconscious attempt to \"stabilize her manifold\" by creating a \"standing wave of consciousness\" to hold her psyche together\nlock\n. Additionally, the source mentions a \"topological betrayal\" that occurred when Nathan attempted to involve an outside doctor in her care, which she perceived as a violation of the \"literal geometry of her safety\"\nlock\n.",
